  "_sourceRefs": [
    "Stedi (stedi.com/edi/edi/hipaa/transaction-set/271-B1) — the HIPAA-specific (005010X279A1) 271 Eligibility, Coverage or Benefit Information (response) transaction set, EDI X12 Phase 3. Same sourcing discipline as 270.json (see its own _sourceRefs) — PyX12 has no 5010/X279 map for this transaction set, sourced from Stedi's own HIPAA-specific guide page instead.",
    "AAA (Request Validation) is the real X12 mechanism a 271 uses to signal a rejection (e.g. subscriber not found) — placed at 2000A, 2100A, 2100B, 2100C, 2100D, 2110C, 2110D per the guide's own explicit table. This engine maps AAA through structurally like any other segment; it never decides WHEN to emit one — that determination belongs to whatever real eligibility system produced the data this transaction set is built from.",
    "FunctionalIdentifierCode 'HB' (Health Care Eligibility Benefit Response) — not yet cross-checked against a live real-world sample; same open confirmation item as 270.json's own GS01/GS08 note.",
    "Named, deliberate simplifications (same as 270.json, plus 271-specific ones): MPI omitted from 2100A-D. TRN (2000C/2000D) reuses the shared, unchanged TRN.json (maxUse stays '1') — same named simplification as 270.json. 2115C/2115D (III, Benefit Additional Information) IS modeled — a normal nested repeating loop, no wrapping complexity.",
    "2120C/2120D (Benefit Related Entity Name) — a later polish pass closed this gap once the engine gained a genuine LS/LE-bracket mechanism (X12LoopDef.Wrapper; edi/loop_engine.go's matchWrappedLoop, edi/builder/segment_writer.go's writeWrappedLoop). Confirmed directly against Stedi's 271-B1 page: contains NM1/N3/N4/PER/PRV (N3/N4/PER/PRV all optional), repeats up to 23, and the LS...LE bracket wraps 2120 ALONE (sibling to, not including, 2115C/2115D) — placed as the last child of 2110C/2110D, after 2115C/2115D, matching the page's own ordering."
  ],
